&lt;h2 id=&#34;description&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#description&#34; class=&#34;header-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    Description
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Jeeves is a fun box that starts with error messages. We directory fuzz with ffuf and find Jenkins running. We gain a foothold with a modifying project exploit that gets us a reverse shell as the user. We see the administrator&amp;rsquo;s hash in the user&amp;rsquo;s KeePass, which gives us a shell with psexec. We get the root flag after discovering the hidden file on the server.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
