        <guid>https://pho3nix-jacki3.github.io/p/law/</guid>
        <description>&lt;img src="https://pho3nix-jacki3.github.io/categories/offsec/offsec-edit.png" alt="Featured image of post Law" /&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://pho3nix-jacki3.github.io/p/law/1.png&#34;
	width=&#34;1834&#34;
	height=&#34;883&#34;
	
	loading=&#34;lazy&#34;
	
	
		class=&#34;gallery-image&#34; 
		data-flex-grow=&#34;207&#34;
		data-flex-basis=&#34;498px&#34;
	
&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;description&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#description&#34; class=&#34;header-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    Description
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;htmLawed 1.2.5 on port 80 of this lab is vulnerable to Remote Code Execution (RCE). We can gain access to the Linux server as the user &amp;lsquo;www-data&amp;rsquo;. We have write access to a cleanup script, which is executed by root. We can use this to escalate our privileges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;skills-learned&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#skills-learned&#34; class=&#34;header-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    Skills Learned
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CVE exploitation &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://mayfly277.github.io/posts/GLPI-htmlawed-CVE-2022-35914/&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;GLPI htmlawed (CVE-2022-35914)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Privilege escalation via cron job&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1 id=&#34;solution&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#solution&#34; class=&#34;header-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    Solution
&lt;/h1&gt;&lt;h2 id=&#34;finding-the-vulnerability&#34;&gt;
    &lt;a href=&#34;#finding-the-vulnerability&#34; class=&#34;header-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;
    Finding the vulnerability
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;autorecon&lt;/code&gt; shows ports 22 and 80 are open.
&lt;br&gt;&lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LkZetyoH2xc&amp;amp;t=10s&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;Video timestamp 0:10&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
        </item>
        <item>
